, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. us-east, us-west and eu-west are all back on it.\n- **Recovery:** the service now passes health checks, and its error rate is 0.2%, down from 18% on v2.3.1.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 says that v2.3.1 failed health checks, that I rolled back to v2.3.0 and that the service recovered. It also says the root cause needs to be found before v2.3.1 is deployed again. There were no existing incidents, so this isn't a duplicate.\n\nThe deploy history shows v2.3.1's release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) was already unhealthy in staging, but it was still deployed to production. You may want to look at how that happened.", "type": "text"}]}]}